{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/942546-is-martial-art-really-that-much-better-than-brawling","id":942546,"title":"is martial art really that much better than brawling?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-03T00:16:32-07:00","id":942546,"title":"is martial art really that much better than brawling?","content":"i mean with all it's maneuvers. i thought that all these things could be done only on chereographed films and that are to impractical to use in a real fight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T00:44:49-07:00","id":942556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/942546-is-martial-art-really-that-much-better-than-brawling#post942546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i mean with all it's maneuvers. i thought that all these things could be done only on chereographed films and that are to impractical to use in a real fight</div> </div> </div> </div>Games aren't Reality simulators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T01:40:42-07:00","id":942571,"title":"","content":"Also not sure which book you're looking at that they're all fake. Learning to dodge and block, lethal blows, those nasty clinches, etc. are the kind of shit people learn in real martial arts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4017,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","user":"angryicecream","date":". 08-03-2016, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T02:37:19-07:00","id":942588,"title":"","content":"The big reason is, of course, that everybody *knows* those maneuvers from choreographed films. They are easily explainable, they are easily applyable, every roleplayer instantly 'gets' them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Describing more practical, real-world martial maneuvers has high situational dependencies that are simply not explicitely happening in normal WoD combat (I.e. 'If somebody strikes at your head from straight ahead with their right hand, and do not have this and that stance, apply a motion that will deflect the force of their blow while positioning yourself in order to apply a lever force to...' )<br /> <br /> Yeah, no thanks.<br /> <br /> Keep it simple. In the end if you do not like the martial arts maneuvers, simply change the names to something you think makes more sense and keep the stats.<br /> <br /> All you did was change semantics, not mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T02:59:09-07:00","id":942597,"title":"","content":"Is the question about the Brawl Ability vs. the Martial Arts Ability (and then which books/editions are we talking about?), or about even the concept of bothering to model them as two different things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T07:11:19-07:00","id":942694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/942546-is-martial-art-really-that-much-better-than-brawling?p=942597#post942597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the question about the Brawl Ability vs. the Martial Arts Ability (and then which books/editions are we talking about?), or about even the concept of bothering to model them as two different things?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> basically the question is &quot;why is martial arts so much better than brawling(e.g kindred of the ease core rulebook and companion i think) when even bruce fucking lee said&quot; an experienced brawler can beat any martial artist&quot;<br /> <br /> honestly it just seems that whenever white wolf wrote a book the word &quot;eastern&quot; might as well as have meant&quot;awesome by default&quot; maybe this was a 1990s thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T07:17:33-07:00","id":942695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/942546-is-martial-art-really-that-much-better-than-brawling?p=942694#post942694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> basically the question is &quot;why is martial arts so much better than brawling(e.g kindred of the ease core rulebook and companion i think) when even bruce fucking lee said&quot; an experienced brawler can beat any martial artist&quot;<br /> <br /> honestly it just seems that whenever white wolf wrote a book the word &quot;eastern&quot; might as well as have meant&quot;awesome by default&quot; maybe this was a 1990s thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>It really isn't. The benefits of the overpriced MA Ability are tiny and easily ignored by most monsters. Hence, likely why the KotE Companion offered a much more restrained and less costly alternative (not that anyone seemed to use it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T09:55:44-07:00","id":942776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/942546-is-martial-art-really-that-much-better-than-brawling?p=942694#post942694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> basically the question is &quot;why is martial arts so much better than brawling(e.g kindred of the ease core rulebook and companion i think) when even bruce fucking lee said&quot; an experienced brawler can beat any martial artist&quot;<br /> <br /> honestly it just seems that whenever white wolf wrote a book the word &quot;eastern&quot; might as well as have meant&quot;awesome by default&quot; maybe this was a 1990s thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I contemplated the same thing when reading M20. It just seems that the old authors, notably Phil in the case of M20 just a little bit biased toward eastern martial arts (and the pop-culture tropes around them and their philosophical angle) and towards non-weapon martial arts. Europe and the west in general (or the middle east, or any other region, really) have at least as rich a martial art heritage as the east, but the eastern-stlye arts have been getting a much better treatment in the WoD books. I mean, in general, I love the M20 book and the artworks in it, but it speaks pages upon pages about martial arts and Do and I dare you to count the katanas in the artworks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I have nothing against eastern arts, or katanas, I'm all into the trenchcoat-katana-good 'ol-gothic-punk-style, but come on! Throw some longswords or rapiers into it! Even the arguably most western traditions the Hermetics and Choristers's pictures are featuring katanas... Mention the more esoterical european styles, for example the Spanish verdadera destreza, medieval german ringen! The oldest fencing tratise we know is from the end of the 13th century and it features a monk, who teaches pupils (among them a woman!) to his unique sword and buckler stlye! I think it is a perfect bit of connection to the Celestial Chorus. Anything, really, just balance the scales a little.<br /> <br /> In fact, I think too it is really a '90s thing in a sense that eastern arts/katanas had a real heyday at that time (too) and influenced WoD naturally. That, and the awareness towards historical western styles, the quantity and quality of their practitioners and our knowledge about them are really boomed in the early-mid 2000's, thanks to the internet (and films like LotR, Kingdom of heaven, etc) and still growing now (The success of GoT and the zillion historical shows also helped to advertise it). So I understand the old books biased state, but it little bit is a sore spot nowadays for me. The best rpg book I read in this whole matter is the NWoD Armory, hands down. <br /> <br /> In general I think NwoD/CofD handles the whole martial styles thing better, the merit system there really enables more room for it. I'd do it in CWoD as something like creating the fighting styles of CofD as Melee and brawl specializations, with certain bonuses, and maneuvers, or something like the CoC skills as secondary skill (maybe with a reduced xp cost). If you want a specified fighting style for specific maneuvers, you take martial arts(italian rapier) for example. Similar to the situation now, but making the secondary skill martial arts an umbrella term and you'll still make rolls with brawl/melee the martial arts skill is just adds certain options and/or bonuses to your repertoire. You can take it several times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T10:21:38-07:00","id":942791,"title":"","content":"Its kind of a false dichotomy really. An experienced brawler <i>is</i> a martial artist, just one without formal systematized training. To use a crude analogy its like comparing someone with an electrical engineering degree to someone with an electrician certificate. Who is going to be better in a given situation? That depends entirely on the requirements of the situation, their experience, and their context-specific knowledge. <br /> <br /> For our purposes its all abstract die-rollers anyway. Martial Arts isn't meant to be objectively better than Brawl in the &quot;real world,&quot; its mechanics are just better within the rules. If we wanted to simulate hand to hand combat realistically we'd have to incorporate Athletics as well and include variable bonuses/penalties for weight and reach. <br /> <br /> We're playing games with supernatural beings anyway, it isn't a stretch to imagine that the Dim Mak Death Touch and the Five Finger Exploding Heart Technique also work in this reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T13:26:15-07:00","id":942948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/942546-is-martial-art-really-that-much-better-than-brawling?p=942694#post942694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">basically the question is &quot;why is martial arts so much better than brawling(e.g kindred of the ease core rulebook and companion i think) when even bruce fucking lee said&quot; an experienced brawler can beat any martial artist&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that this question is more complex than you're treating it.<br /> <br /> I see two core things.<br /> <br /> 1) Why does the system model &quot;basic&quot; fighting in the form of Brawl and Melee, as well as specialist fighting in the form of various supplemental Abilities (Do, Martial Arts, Blind Fighting, Klaviskar, Ikkaksu, etc.)?<br /> <br /> 2) Why might some of those things be mechanically superior to the others.<br /> <br /> The first is a lot more complicated than comparing costs/benefits. Some of the answers make sense from a design standpoint (Blind Fighting is a specialized skill even among fighters, so it makes sense as something certain characters would develop separate from basic fighting skills), while others make sense from a setting perspective (Do is a magical fighting practice that does things better because magic), and others are more questionable (Martial Arts was introduced more as 90s action than fulfilling a design niche or setting concern).<br /> <br /> The second question requires establishing if and when this is even the case, before establishing if it should be the case. Martial Arts in KotE core isn't significantly superior to Brawl, but is definitely superior to Brawl in M20. Do has always been better than Brawl, but it's supposed to be because, again, magic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T16:55:25-07:00","id":943111,"title":"","content":"The question should be more why does WoD combat suck so bad. Nearly every martial arts, unless it is a pure art ot sport style, teaches how to defend against weapons, but it has long been a thing in WoD that unarmed fighters cannot use Brawl to defend against Melee attacks. Then you have the inability to specifically cripple limbs, which minimizes the effectiveness of an unarmed fighter even further. MA was just an overpriced way to try to fix the imbalance, similar to WoD combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:25:26-07:00","id":943336,"title":"","content":"I always thought what Brawl lacked in maneuvers it made up in the easier use of improvised weapons like chairs and bottles etc. Maybe that's just the way I do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T23:06:32-07:00","id":943434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/942546-is-martial-art-really-that-much-better-than-brawling?p=943111#post943111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nearly every martial arts, unless it is a pure art ot sport style, teaches how to defend against weapons, but it has long been a thing in WoD that unarmed fighters cannot use Brawl to defend against Melee attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't apply the Block maneuver against weapons based attacks, because that's trying to stop a blade with your arm... it just means getting your arm cut up.<br /> <br /> Combat training wouldn't just mean &quot;Brawl&quot; training in the first place, since it should include Dodge/Athletics (aka the Dodge maneuver, which can be applied to hand-to-hand weapons for normal folks) in general.<br /> <br /> As well, you can use Brawl to fend off Melee, it just means using actual self-defense tactics; like disarming the target (which you can do by striking their hand, or by grappling where high Brawl is king).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then you have the inability to specifically cripple limbs, which minimizes the effectiveness of an unarmed fighter even further. </div> </div> </div>There is no such inability. Called shots to limbs works with Brawl. It's less effective in general since it'll probably be bashing instead of lethal, but that's part of the differentiation between them. If you want to permanently ruin someone's leg, a shotgun is better than your bare hands. It doesn't mean you can't with your hands (esp. if you know what you're doing), just that it's harder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/942546-is-martial-art-really-that-much-better-than-brawling?p=943336#post943336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought what Brawl lacked in maneuvers it made up in the easier use of improvised weapons like chairs and bottles etc. Maybe that's just the way I do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on book/edition, Brawl isn't really lacking in maneuvers (though MA has better ones), and Brawl gets its either automatically, or at Brawl 3 depending on book/edition. Improvised weapons is more of a Exalted Brawl thing.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T04:16:43-07:00","id":943531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/942546-is-martial-art-really-that-much-better-than-brawling?p=943434#post943434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can't apply the Block maneuver against weapons based attacks, because that's trying to stop a blade with your arm... it just means getting your arm cut up.<br /> <br /> Combat training wouldn't just mean &quot;Brawl&quot; training in the first place, since it should include Dodge/Athletics (aka the Dodge maneuver, which can be applied to hand-to-hand weapons for normal folks) in general.<br /> <br /> As well, you can use Brawl to fend off Melee, it just means using actual self-defense tactics; like disarming the target (which you can do by striking their hand, or by grappling where high Brawl is king).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There is no such inability. Called shots to limbs works with Brawl. It's less effective in general since it'll probably be bashing instead of lethal, but that's part of the differentiation between them. If you want to permanently ruin someone's leg, a shotgun is better than your bare hands. It doesn't mean you can't with your hands (esp. if you know what you're doing), just that it's harder.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Depending on book/edition, Brawl isn't really lacking in maneuvers (though MA has better ones), and Brawl gets its either automatically, or at Brawl 3 depending on book/edition. Improvised weapons is more of a Exalted Brawl thing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> which books gives you maneuvers if you have brawl 3?<br /> <br /> as for the basic maneuvers listed in the core rulebooks for brawl im pretty sure one with martial arts is capeble of doing them as well. kote doesn't mention them simply because they don't have a different difficulty.<br /> <br /> i mean is a martial artist really incapable of doing &quot;sweep&quot; or tackle&quot; ?<br /> <br /> unless there has been some online ruling i missed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T08:29:26-07:00","id":943645,"title":"","content":"You can stop a blade with your arms, you just step inside and knock aside the wrist or forearm. That is basic martial arts training, what is called Brawl in WoD, which does not require any special abilities. You can even do it to a person with a pistol, if they are stupid enough to allow you to get close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T09:00:58-07:00","id":943661,"title":"","content":"I think it shouldn't be. Throwing a punch at a moving target is always brawl, never martial arts. I'm of the opinion that fighting should be houseruled. The WoD combat system is one of way too many dice and slow turns, but the d10 system so much better than rolling one dice for complicated manovuers. <br /> <br /> The problem is people need to know the complex manovuers or at least have some creativity/ sense of how to fight. problem with one of my storytellers/players is that I've been in a few fights and trained in a few styles. I'm not a pro or anything really good, i just did this stuff when I was a kid/Teen- he's a couch potato who watches WWE. <br /> <br /> When I'm storyteller, I tend to tweak the combat rules to make them more 'real'. IE holding the enemy is a contested action and the dice you get over the enemy dictates an advantage you get in further melee actions. Hitting certain places affects the difficulty of damage/soak rolls. I add/takeaway dice/difficulty for a bunch of little things to compensate for everything so it all makes sense. Problem is half my players just wanna 'claw it'. I suppose you need people with an interest in how things work, but it's not exactly like players just wanting to claw it have taken away from anything. <br /> <br /> He relies on the rulebook, and things go awry if they're not in the rules. Wrestling moves (many of which are designed to not be as painful as they look, in the event they look painful) are the only thing you'll get more elaborate than what's in the books, and they'l be fluff rather than mechanics. Hitting someone in the right place usualy won't do something special. most troubling is that taking the trouble to shoot someone in the head with a gun is +2 difficulty to hit, with a chance to stun them (dictated by a d2). It's never really worth it unless you're fighting a vampire. <br /> <br /> <br /> But, a martial arts skill... I feel like a martial arts skill is more of a 'look at these moves i know'. I'd do something like<br /> Here's a few moves, difficulty 9. <br /> Learn the martial arts skill to reduce their difficulty by up to three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:15:41-07:00","id":943808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/942546-is-martial-art-really-that-much-better-than-brawling?p=943531#post943531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">which books gives you maneuvers if you have brawl 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any the have a Dirty Fighting section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> as for the basic maneuvers listed in the core rulebooks for brawl im pretty sure one with martial arts is capeble of doing them as well. kote doesn't mention them simply because they don't have a different difficulty. </div> </div> </div>Correct, in the books that use MA, they have access to general maneuvers. Basically, Brawl gets Dirty Fighting, and MA gets customized special maneuvers as what mechanically separates them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/942546-is-martial-art-really-that-much-better-than-brawling?p=943645#post943645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can stop a blade with your arms, you just step inside and knock aside the wrist or forearm. That is basic martial arts training, what is called Brawl in WoD, which does not require any special abilities. You can even do it to a person with a pistol, if they are stupid enough to allow you to get close.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love, &quot;you can block a blade by not blocking the blade,&quot; as a counter.<br /> <br /> 1) Combat training is not &quot;Brawl&quot; training, because as I've mentioned, Athletics/Dodge at a minimum are parts of basic unarmed training as well. Just like going to a four year university and majoring in a science degree isn't just getting your dots in Science, but also Academics at a minimum (if not lots of other things depending on your minor, electives, and clubs).<br /> <br /> 2) I already addressed how the system models trying to stop a melee or firearms attack with Brawl. It just isn't with the Block maneuver. You really need to stop conflating jargon (the specific use of a word in a specific context) with general use. The Block maneuver does not cover everything that in common use might be called a &quot;block.&quot; I can &quot;block&quot; someone trying to punch me with a staff, but in the system that's the Parry maneuver, not the Block maneuver. If you want to stop someone with a knife or a pistol, and you're unarmed, you don't use the Block maneuver, even if you want to describe a called shot to their arm an attempt to &quot;block&quot; their strike. The mechanical significance of this though, is that you can't do this as a default defensive action (so you can't abort to it), which means having Initiative is really important to trying anti-weapon unarmed tactics; which makes complete sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/942546-is-martial-art-really-that-much-better-than-brawling?p=943661#post943661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hitting certain places affects the difficulty of damage/soak rolls. I add/takeaway dice/difficulty for a bunch of little things to compensate for everything so it all makes sense. Problem is half my players just wanna 'claw it'.</div> </div> </div> </div>These might not be unrelated; especially if you modify difficulties on things like damage/soak.<br /> <br /> This adds even more variables to combat, which leads to decision paralysis, which can be avoided by just skipping any non-basic combat options.<br /> <br /> I think if you want to encourage more that, &quot;I claw it,&quot; it needs to be easier to know why to try other options. The current system is bad enough. Most players don't know if trading +1 diff for +1 damage is worth it or not. The cWOD combat system would benefit more from a simple maneuver creation system instead of pages of maneuvers. Explaining how to build maneuvers also helps explain when to use them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T01:35:30-07:00","id":944189,"title":"","content":"i jsut lookes at the dirty fighting section and...honestly it seems ridiculous to me. not the techniques mind you but rather the fact that you need a brawl rating of 3 to do them and that martial arts can't do them.<br /> <br /> <br /> do you really need some super special training to stomp someone's face when they are down? or lift something lighter than you and throw it down? or claw someone's face?<br /> <br /> i mean i have a brawl rating of 0 and i could propably do these things<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T03:51:37-07:00","id":944221,"title":"","content":"MA can't do them, but almost universally has something better anyway (though not every MA user will have every maneuver, unlike Dirty Fighting).<br /> <br /> And most of the Dirty Fighting moves are minor bonuses over general moves. Most of them can be easily replicated with just a called shot and a normal strike or something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T06:42:45-07:00","id":944277,"title":"","content":"Blocking a weapon has nothing to do with Dodge/Athleticism. It has everything to do with your skill in Brawl because you use many of the same techniques to defend against a weapon that you would use to defend against a punch or kick. The difference is that failure is much, much more painful.<br /> <br /> Most combat styles teach weapon blocking and disarming techniques to allow their students to gain access to the weapon of the opponent. They usually consist of step in, block the weapon by deflecting the angle of attack with your hands, grab the wrists, and disarm the opponent (usually by breaking the wrists). You can then pick up the weapon for your own use or proceed to destroy the formerly armed opponent. The schools I have been associated with usually preferred the latter, as there was no guarantee that they did not have a second weapon. Destroying a person usually focuses on crippling the second arm and one leg, generally taking two more attacks, rather than more serious damage because someone with just one good limb was not a threat and it takes a really long time to beat someone into Unconscious, much longer than suggested by WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T11:57:00-07:00","id":944440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/942546-is-martial-art-really-that-much-better-than-brawling?p=943645#post943645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can stop a blade with your arms, you just step inside and knock aside the wrist or forearm. That is basic martial arts training, what is called Brawl in WoD, which does not require any special abilities. You can even do it to a person with a pistol, if they are stupid enough to allow you to get close.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Me parrying your attack doesn't mean i need to block your BLADE (or club).. BUT stop your arm/hand holding the weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T13:17:33-07:00","id":944490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/942546-is-martial-art-really-that-much-better-than-brawling?p=944277#post944277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blocking a weapon has nothing to do with Dodge/Athleticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... it does. As you illustrate one of the first steps is positioning and foot-work, which are covered by Dodge and/or Athletics depending on the edition/book we're using.<br /> <br /> Ok, I'm going to break this down in mechanical terms:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They usually consist of step in,... </div> </div> </div>Either you've won Initiative and are using your reflexive movement, or you lost Initiative and are using the Evasive Action maneuver (Athletics!) to position yourself advantageously for your following move (Evasive Action isn't just avoiding a blow, but doing so in a fashion that nets you a mechanical benefit for a follow up counter if you avoid the attack completely).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> block the weapon by deflecting the angle of attack with your hands, grab the wrists, </div> </div> </div>Initiate a grapple, denying the opponent the ability to attack with their weapon unless they can out grapple you as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and disarm the opponent (usually by breaking the wrists). </div> </div> </div>Either use the disarm option in a grapple, take control of the weapons (see next section), or make a called shot in the grapple against their arm/wrist to do enough damage to make them drop the weapon anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can then pick up the weapon for your own use or proceed to destroy the formerly armed opponent. </div> </div> </div>Either using the weapon after taking control over it, or not, use the grappling option to damage them until you're satisfied they can't fight back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The schools I have been associated with usually preferred the latter, as there was no guarantee that they did not have a second weapon. Destroying a person usually focuses on crippling the second arm and one leg, generally taking two more attacks, rather than more serious damage because someone with just one good limb was not a threat and it takes a really long time to beat someone into Unconscious, much longer than suggested by WoD. </div> </div> </div>The idea that two broken wrists/arms and a broken leg isn't &quot;serious&quot; damage on par with being beaten unconscious is... a bit of a questionable assumption. But the system doesn't model damage in such fine detail anyway. Besides putting most people in the Crippled damage level (-5 to their actions) will either net them zero dice and auto-fail any attacks (as well as move so slow you can easily out run them if they're using hand-to-hand weapons), or a small enough dice pool finishing the job if they keep fighting shouldn't be a problem. And this is technically easier than putting them into Incapacitated - which would be beating them unconscious - since it takes less damage.<br /> <br /> And, again, you don't have to think of this as the optimal way of handling it in the system. The core point I'm making here is that the self-defense/combat tactics you're talking about are in the system, even if they're not in the &quot;Block&quot; maneuver. They're not impossible to do RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T19:21:18-07:00","id":944656,"title":"","content":"I just want to add to my previous post (because I'm still reading through HDYDT), that it is indeed mentions European martial traditions (fencing, notably and it's connection to mathematics), which I'm applauding, it's a big plus for me (and indeed the description of the melee skill in the corebook is also absolutely solid), but I think my statements are still holding, that in the artworks and regarding the amount of space spend in rules there is a big leaning to the side of non-weapon and Eastern arts. Like, there are dozens of maneuvers for them and weapons only had simple striking, parrying, disarming and that's it. I could imagine some more, like feints, striking with the hilt, lunging, circular striking, one-tempo defense-attacks, etc. It's not that these are necessary, the covered parts are enough for playing, but it's a bit annoying that hand-to-hand gets a LOT more nuanced treatment. I'm a little puzzled why is that, since Phil obviously familiar with (or at least aware of) a wide range of subjects, so I don't 'blame' him personally. I could only rationalize it as remnants of the earlier editions (and that era's knowledge and pop culture - see my earlier post), since it's been this way in every CWoD corebook I saw, both 20th or earlier.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T23:56:53-07:00","id":944739,"title":"","content":"It's pretty much always been that way. WtA and DAV Revised were the only games to give Melee equal love. WtA locked it in some specialized skills (like CoG staff fighting and Klaive dueling). DA just had more options in the default list.<br /> <br /> I think some of it is just that weapons (esp. against anything without lethal soak) are potent enough that basic strikes can be so devastating that special moves aren't really needed, while Brawl defaulting to Bashing (and no access to high damage weapons) got maneuvers in a fairly ill conceived attempt at balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T14:03:32-07:00","id":945051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/942546-is-martial-art-really-that-much-better-than-brawling?p=944739#post944739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty much always been that way. WtA and DAV Revised were the only games to give Melee equal love. WtA locked it in some specialized skills (like CoG staff fighting and Klaive dueling). DA just had more options in the default list.<br /> <br /> I think some of it is just that weapons (esp. against anything without lethal soak) are potent enough that basic strikes can be so devastating that special moves aren't really needed, while Brawl defaulting to Bashing (and no access to high damage weapons) got maneuvers in a fairly ill conceived attempt at balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be also that, I like your reasoning, however I'm also still holding up the historical one. I might add that, if what you wrote was, or part of the reason, it was indeed ill-conceived. Maneuvers should be situational applications, an increase in flexibility instead of power, IMO. And, well, I think balancing the two is pointless, because weapons ARE better, than bare hands. Every sane MA enthusiast/instructor/self-defence instructor/etc can tell that, that's why we've been using them from the dawn of mankind. Brawling is for the occasion when for some reason you don't or can't have any weapon (like, well, a large part of the modern world, but in certain cities/countries in historical times also, but it's a big topic...). The only occasion when I could justify the balancing of the two is regarding supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> I never get into the DA stuff, not because I'm uninterested, more like there were always more books and games to read which I had the bigger chance to actually use. But I will check out them, thanks! I knew about the WtA ones, but not in depth.<br /> <br /> I might add, that really, I'm not complaining often about the CWoD rules (and I love the setting), I'm mostly okay with them. I think the CofD has the, not necessarily &quot;better&quot;, but simpler, faster more streamlined core rules, which I nowadays seeing more as a sidegrade than a strict upgrade. Although one part where NWoD-CofD is strictly better in my eyes is the mechanical handling of merits (however I like the CWoD merit-flaw distinction) and especially the handling of fighting styles, it's flexible and open-ended and Armory was indeed the best rpg supplement I saw on the topic (I'm waiting curiously for Hurt Locker). If I'd be the WW staff, I'd aim for something similar in the new ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}